# Backend (migrated from FastAPI)

Backend lives in this Next.js app as **App Router Route Handlers** under `src/app/api/v1/`. The Python FastAPI app (`mira_project`) is no longer required for local/prod serving.

## Layout

- Routes: `src/app/api/v1/chat/...`
  - `POST .../conversations/danny/completions` — SSE chat stream
  - `POST .../conversations` — create conversation
- Server modules: `src/server/` (`db/`, `chat/`, `ai/`)
- Client API helpers remain in `src/shared/` and call same-origin `/api/v1`

## Contract

- Completions stream SSE with the existing `/&` framing (`metadata`, `message`, `[DONE]`)
- Threading uses `parent_id` / `assistant_message_id`
- Messages stored in MongoDB `danny_messages` with a TTL index on `ttl` (30 min expiry)
- Conversation reconstruction uses `$graphLookup` (do not reintroduce full-collection scans)
- LLM via OpenRouter (`openai` SDK + `baseURL: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`)
- Resume is a static file at `/resume.pdf` (not an API route)
- Telegram notify and title generation are intentionally not ported

## Contextual AI

- The request body may include optional `context_type` (`"project" | "experience"`) and `context_id`; the completions route passes them to `generateCompletion(messages, { type, id })`
- `@src/server/ai/context.ts` (`resolveContextBlock`, `validSourceSlugs`) resolves an id to a fact block from `@src/shared/projects.ts` / `@src/shared/profile.ts` — returns `null` on an unknown id so the assistant falls back to a general answer instead of erroring
- `getSystemPrompt(context?)` in `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` appends the resolved `<CURRENT_CONTEXT>` block and instructs the model to end relevant replies with `[[LINK:project:<slug>]]` / `[[LINK:experience:<id>]]` markers (parsed client-side by `@src/lib/sourceLinks.ts`); only slugs/ids from `validSourceSlugs()` are valid — never let the model invent one
- Context is per-request only; it is not required to persist beyond the stored message's optional `context_type`/`context_id` fields

## Validation and deps

- Validate request bodies with zod schemas in `src/server/chat/schemas.ts`
- Prefer idiomatic Node/Next patterns over literal Python ports

## Env (server-only)

- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
- `MONGO_CONNECTION_STRING`, `MONGO_DATABASE`
- Chat model list lives in `src/server/ai/modelRotation.ts` (not env); 429/402/5xx triggers in-memory cooldown fallback across the registry
